# Feature structure

Each product area is one folder under `frontend/src/features`. A feature owns its pages, components, hooks, API calls, and schemas.

```text
src/features/workOrders/
  api/workOrders.api.ts
  components/AssignTechnicianForm.tsx
  hooks/useAssignWorkOrder.ts
  pages/WorkOrderDetailPage.tsx
  schemas/assignWorkOrder.schema.ts
  index.ts
src/components/ui/          # shadcn primitives only
src/components/             # shared across two or more features
src/lib/                    # api client, auth, formatting
src/routes/
```

- A page composes feature components and hooks. It does not call `fetch` or the API client directly.
- Keep a component inside its feature until a second feature imports it, then move it to `src/components`.
- `src/components/ui` is generated primitives. Do not put business logic there.
- Route files only map paths to pages.
- Component files are PascalCase. Hooks are `useX.ts`. Everything else is camelCase.
